Map memory-mapped weights through the compute device's own host-pointer buffer.

Submitted upstream as https://github.com/leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp/pull/2037; drop this patch once
the pinned commit includes it.

sd.cpp enables mmap when the compute backend can wrap host memory (Metal on unified memory), but it
always wraps the mapping in a CPU buffer. Metal kernels cannot address a CPU buffer, and nothing
stages the weights because the params backend already is the compute backend, so every mapped
weight fails with "ggml_metal_buffer_get_id: error: tensor ... buffer is nil" and the output is
garbage. This maps each file once per device with buffer_from_host_ptr (Metal wraps the mapping
without copying it) and lets the loader skip reading those tensors, as it does for CPU mappings.
Writable mappings, used when LoRAs are merged in place, are left to the normal loading path.

Applied by scripts/build-sdcpp-xcframework.sh on top of the pinned stable-diffusion.cpp commit.

